# PUSH — local environment template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in this same folder (or just edit the `.env` that's
# already sitting here) and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored — see the
# root .gitignore (`.env` / `.env.*` patterns) — nothing here ever reaches the
# public repo. This file (`.env.example`) has no real values and is safe to commit.
#
# These keys are needed in up to TWO places, not just here. This file is a
# single staging spot to fill them in once; where each one also needs to be
# copied to is noted per line.
#
# An earlier design considered an n8n-based front door as an alternative to the
# GitHub Actions cron poller (push-poll.yml). That path was never built; the
# cron poller is what actually runs. n8n-specific vars (GH_WORKFLOW_DISPATCH_TOKEN,
# N8N_HOST, N8N_API_KEY) were removed from this file for that reason — nothing
# in the current codebase consumes them, and keeping unused credential fields
# around only invites filling them in with real, unnecessary secrets. See
# LEARNING.md, 2026-08-07, for the audit that found this.

# --- Telegram bot ---
# Create via @BotFather on Telegram (`/newbot`). Use a dedicated bot for PUSH,
# not one shared with any other webhook-based integration: Telegram will not
# allow a bot to use getUpdates (what push-bridge.sh and push-poll.yml both do)
# while any webhook is registered on it, and the conflict fails silently in
# push-poll.yml's own error handling (see LEARNING.md, 2026-08-07). One bot,
# one PUSH instance.
# Also needed as: GitHub repo secret (push-poll.yml, push-dispatch.yml).
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Your personal numeric chat ID — the bot only ever acts on messages from this
# ID. Get it by messaging @userinfobot, or: send your new bot one message,
# then read the numeric chat.id off the first inbound update.
# Also needed as: GitHub repo secret.
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# --- Anthropic (either one, not both required) ---
# The headless cold-start path (push-dispatch.yml) needs one of these two.
# Preferred: CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN — draws against a Pro/Max subscription
# instead of metered API billing. Generate it by running `claude setup-token`
# in YOUR OWN terminal (it opens a browser for OAuth login — cannot be run
# from inside a Claude Code session on your behalf). Valid for 1 year. Paste
# the result here, then it becomes the GitHub repo secret.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Fallback: metered API billing instead of subscription usage. Get one at
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys. Only needed if you're not
# using CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: Telegram-driven ship approval (SETUP.md section 7) ---
# Only needed if you want to approve/reject a `ship` job by replying in
# Telegram instead of GitHub's own UI/Mobile app (which needs nothing here
# at all — a completely valid choice). A classic PAT (full `repo` scope,
# required by the pending_deployments endpoint — confirmed against GitHub's
# docs, no narrower scope covers it), generated under a SEPARATE, dedicated
# GitHub account added as a second required reviewer on weaponx-approval —
# never your primary account's token. See SETUP.md section 7 for the full
# setup. Deleting this secret is an instant kill switch back to
# GitHub-UI/Mobile-only approval; nothing else about PUSH changes.
# Also needed as: GitHub repo secret (push-poll.yml only — never exposed to
# push-dispatch.yml's `run` job, which executes semi-trusted generated code).
WEAPONX_APPROVAL_REVIEWER_PAT=
